<div class="center-column">
  <p>
    When connected to a GitHub repository, you can take advantage of several
    <strong>automations</strong>. Simply add a Applications Integration to the repo owner's
    GitHub account, then copy the generated API key to an environment variable of your
    TaskRoller app.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="columns">
  <div class="half-column">
    <dl class="integration-list">
      <dt>Issue Import</dt>
      <dd>
        Issues added to GitHub are sent to your TaskRoller instance and updated with automatic
        comments when the status is changed. In addition, the GitHub Issue is closed after the
        App's Issue is closed. If the GitHub user has an App account with the same
        email address, the Issue is associated with them. Conversely, a new user is added to
        the App which could allow them to later log in.
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <div class="half-column">
    <div class="image-wrapper">
      <img src="/images/screenshot-github-integration-import.png" alt="Import Example">
      <p class="image-label">Issue Imported from GitHub</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="columns">
  <div class="half-column">
    <dl class="integration-list">
      <dt>Commit Message Callouts</dt>
      <dd>
        Tasks can be transitioned automatically just by adding a <strong>callout</strong> to
        the repo's commit message, like <code>"Fixes Task#112"</code>. The only requirement is
        users must connect their GitHub account to the app in their "Account Settings". Here
        are the possible state changes:

        <ul>
          <li><strong class="color-green">Start/Progress</strong> <%= icon('arrow-right') %> Start working on Task</li>
          <li><strong class="color-yellow">Pause</strong> <%= icon('arrow-right') %> Pause working on Task</li>
          <li><strong class="color-red">Fix/Close/Complete</strong> <%= icon('arrow-right') %> Mark Task is ready for review</li>
        </ul>
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <div class="half-column">
    <div class="image-wrapper">
      <img src="/images/screenshot-github-integration-callout.png" alt="Callout Example">
      <p class="image-label">Commit Message</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
